# Security policy

## Supported versions

Security fixes go into the latest release only. On an older one, the fix is to
upgrade: nothing is backported.

## Reporting a vulnerability

Report it privately, through GitHub:
<https://github.com/{{ repo }}/security/advisories/new>

Please do not open an issue, a pull request or a discussion about it. Until a
fix is released, a public report helps whoever reads it first, and that is not
always the maintainers.

A report that can be acted on says:

- which version is affected - the release, or the commit you built from;
- what an attacker can do with it, and what they need before they can;
- the shortest way to reproduce it.

The answer comes in the advisory itself. Once a fix is released the advisory
is published, crediting you unless you would rather not be named.

If the link says private reporting is not enabled for this repository, open an
issue asking for a private contact - with no details of the problem in it.
